# V14 prepass r2 at 400p — less noise, horizon edge, Gargantua orbit flow, lensing

Coordinate: 23.7.10/8.8.11/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 22:45 CST
Request (verbatim): V14 is on the right track again - tweaks: a little less noise; treat the wavefront as forming the edge of an event horizon - Interstellar's Gargantua as inspiration for how the orbits flow - gravitational lensing makes our effective influence larger than expected. Run another prepass at 400p w/ those tweaks
Status: completed — r2 prepass delivered and coordinator-verified

Notes:
- Parent: 34.8.9/9.9.12/7.7.10 (360p prepass). Will's verdict on r1: on the right track again.
- Tweak readings (Emise, to be measured in the build): less noise = film grain down one step (constant read from the code, ~x0.65), snow stays; orbit flow = Kepler-style shear (inner faster) with the median radius keeping the 45-degree reading; lensing = projection bend away from the centre, capped and smooth, field layer only, so the wavefront's reach reads larger than its true size; horizon edge must come from the lensing/shear itself, no drawn ring.
- P3* placement unchanged in r2; builder re-measures its framing under the new flow and reports — no forcing it into frame.
- Untweaked prep held r1 exactly (731 pool, 169 segments, same OU seed, same P3*) — the three tweaks are the only changes. One build deviation, owned in the report: first r2 pass ran rho=256, which put the median point at 90% of the lensing cap against the brief's rule; retuned to rho=128 and re-rendered, discarded pass kept on the node and its cost counted.
- P3* re-check on r2: shear pulled it ~3-7 degrees closer (pull-back 29.0-39.4 deg off axis, CTA 28.2-29.6) but still 0 of 440 frames in frame, closest ~69-75 px below the bottom edge. The end-point call is still Will's, unchanged.

Results:
- files/v14-build/v14-prepass-400p.mp4 — 299,326,069 B, SHA-256 f66e5370a4c75564b36904d65bf8d60aeb340bc734258b7718d8e1795279a2da (same on aletheia-core, this VM, Elven Path; coordinator re-measured). Staged: https://elven-path.pizzly-halfmoon.ts.net/v14-prepass-400p.mp4 (HTTP 206 passed).
- Tweaks measured: grain GRAIN_SIG 5.2 -> 3.38 (x0.65); dark-tile grain sigma 3.899 (r1) -> 2.776 (r2). Kepler shear: r_med 0.402 over 6,485 points, angle over film p10 125.4 / p50 45.0 / p90 20.6 degrees. Lensing at f2400: median bend 30.5 px (4.3% of width), p90 39.8, cap 42.7 px; field layer only, no ring drawn.
