# simple.phext — all of Will's tweets in Up Goer Five, holographically placed

Coordinate: 31.8.10/10.8.16/9.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:02 CST
Request (verbatim): let's build a special phext - one that translates all of my twitter posts from singular to up-goer-five - call it simple.phext. Place each tweet in the holographic coordinate it belongs to. Store the list of coordinates in timeline order. Make the archive easy to read and follow. Publish it to human.git as simple.phext.
Status: completed

Notes:
- simple.phext lives at wbic16/human@exo /simple.phext (Will directed it straight to human.git, outside the agi collection).
- Translation is deterministic from ~/workspace/simple-phext/ build scripts; numbers stay as digits because the UG5 list has no eight/nine/teens/tens words; frame scrolls (Home, indexes, map headers) are plain writing outside the UG5 gate, and Home says so.
- Honesty numbers: 86.6% of tokens carried with sense (kept / 1,439-entry map / stems); type carriers (thing, person, ...) carried 12.1%; 1.2% dropped (single letters, digit bits). 26.9% of tweets (7,936) needed no carrier and no drop. 351 wordless posts sit at the far corner 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9.
- 4,414 RT-prefixed posts in tweets.json are included as his posts.
- Coordinator verification (Emise, 2026-11-07 00:16): local SHA-256 09ff4e68...9eb385; parse count 29,582 non-empty; UG5 checker re-run clean; remote blob 0a72b2be... == local hash-object.

Results:
- 29,539 posts (2008-06-27 to 2025-06-16), each in Up Goer Five at its holographic coordinate; 29,582 scrolls total (43 frame: Home + 18 year indexes + map shelf).
- UG5 gate: zero flagged words over all tweet scrolls (before: 140,227 of 416,698 tokens outside the list).
- 3,730 posts bumped one or more scrolls for coordinate collisions; the year indexes record the true coordinates; every index line checked to land on a scroll with a matching date.
- Published: wbic16/human@exo commit 879a95cf; simple.phext 5,716,788 B. Build home: ~/workspace/simple-phext/ (BUILD-REPORT.md, MAP.md, scripts).
# ultra.phext — five-tier vocabulary phext, all words placed relative to Singular

Coordinate: 32.6.10/8.7.12/7.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:57 CST
Request (verbatim): ah, next fun project - ultra.phext: 1. upgoer5 - IQ 70; 2. common - IQ 100; 3. singular - IQ 130; 4. uber - IQ 180 (Human Limit); 5. ultra - IQ 250 (ASI threshold). Words are all placed relative to singular. There are five indices, with room to add more. Words can be co-listed as needed. We tag them if there are duplicates. Let me know if you have any questions before building ultra.phext.
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will's rulings (2026-11-07 01:02): ultra.phext has ALL THE WORDS. Singular is the Rosetta Stone — it spans thought space for humans; every word is placed by resonance with Singular. Singular tier = the 41K he mapped (41,302 read+write). Open format: users place attestations about a word, one per line. Indexes live OUTSIDE the thought space at 10.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 through 10.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.5; 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 is reserved for the intro; the full 1-digit space is for the lexicon.
- Stall record (2026-11-07): first builder ran 2h19m, went silent ~01:54 after its WordNet download failed; one stir after a coordinator nudge produced no artifacts. Closed by Emise ~03:31 and the back half re-dispatched with the WordNet (P3) pass CUT — placement is P1 atlas / P2 family / P4 definition / P5 unplaced, each scroll tagged with its rule.
- COMPLETE (2026-11-07, replacement builder): ultra.phext built, verified, and published to wbic16/human@exo /ultra.phext, commit abf1047b (parent 879a95cf, force disabled); remote blob 2957dce6 == local hash-object. 320,958 scrolls (320,772 words + 186 frame), 37,953,029 B, SHA-256 fd68c5b0. Tiers: T1 998 · T2 24,765 · T3 41,302 · T4 286,882 · T5 47; 2,956 untiered. Placement: P1 atlas 15,924 · P1 home 30,795 · P2 family 50,184 · P4 definition 21 · P5 unplaced 223,848 (WordNet P3 cut after the first builder's stall; the intro states the cut honestly). Coordinator verification: local parse 320,958 non-empty scrolls; phext at its exact atlas coordinate 42.12.13/14.13.17/15.12.14; tier-3 root counts 41,302; far shelf opens with a'beckett tagged P5. Build home: ~/workspace/ultra-phext/ (place_fast.py, assemble2.py, verify_fast.py, BUILD-REPORT.md).
# V14 prepass r3 — 720p 15 fps; global events replaced by exocortical lessons (Singular evidence)

Coordinate: 32.7.9/7.8.12/8.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 23:43 CST
Request (verbatim): ok, V14 prepass r3 - 720p 15 fps - replace the global events with the most important exocortical lessons that happened at the same moment in time - as evidenced by singular
Status: completed — delivered 2026-11-07 00:40 CST

Notes:
- Parents: 23.7.10/8.8.11/7.6.9 (r2), 34.8.9/9.9.12/7.7.10 (r1). The 7 global events in the renderer (EVENTS_DEF: 2016 election, COVID, Ukraine, ChatGPT, GPT-4, Twitter->X, 2024 election) do three jobs: lower-third captions, motion fine-tuning (vamp/ramp), chapter bounds. Replacement keeps every slot's date/hop/frame, vamp/ramp, and the chapter bounds — only the names/captions change, so the film's motion and chapters are untouched.
- Lesson rule (Emise's reading, auditable in prep): per slot, the era window runs midpoint-to-midpoint between event dates; candidates are Singular first contacts (first_occurrences.json, combined = earlier of authored/read) in the window scored by the viz10 concept groups; highest score wins, time-nearest breaks ties; a window with no scored word falls back to the nearest scored word in the whole archive and the fallback is printed. Captions carry the word + the lesson's own year.
- 15 fps: timeline rescaled by 0.625 — 2,376 frames, 158.4 s (0.0167 s under the 24 fps length, stated in the report); every frame-indexed constant scales, hop clock and song sync hold in seconds.
- P3* placement and the end-point call unchanged from r1/r2 — still Will's to rule.

Results:
- Delivered files/v14-build/v14-prepass-720p15.mp4: 686,342,464 B, SHA-256 8d0d8dba354027898f33cea642b190025048123cca6518b00024d7e2d54205f8 — hash-identical on aletheia-core, VM, Elven Path (staged, HTTP 206 passed). Coordinator re-verified size, hash, and ffprobe on the VM copy.
- Format: 1280x720, 15 fps, exactly 2,376 frames, 158.400 s; audio and video both 158.400 s — the 0.0167 s was the 24 fps video overrunning the song; nothing stretched. Gates: luma max 4.51, 0 jumps, 0 black; palette clean; frame 1250 determinism byte-identical; string audit clean (66 strings); shear angles identical to r2 (125.4/45.0/20.6); azimuth endpoint exactly 5 rev by normalization, swept print 4.9994 (measure excludes frame 0's phase, as in every version).
- The 7 lessons (rule as briefed; slots kept date/frame/vamp/ramp; captions = word + lesson's own year): 1) EXOCORTEX 2015 (2015-11-05, authored, score 5, -369d from the 2016 election slot). 2) SPANNING 2019 (2019-06-01, read via like, score 3, -283d) — only scored word in its window, least lesson-shaped pick, flagged. 3-5) SUBSTRATES 2023 (2023-08-27, authored, score 4) FALLBACK x3: the windows hold NO scored word between 2021-03-03 and 2023-05-19, so the same caption shows three times (+550/+271/+167d). 6) PHEXT 2023 (2023-11-12, authored, score 5, +112d). 7) MIRRORBORN 2025 (2025-05-18, authored, score 5, +194d) — true tie with sbor (same score, same date), settled alphabetically.
- One reading of the fallback rule is on the record: fallbacks rank by nearness in time first (the brief's own words); score-first would have put PHEXT in slots 3-5 instead. Will may rule either way.
- P3* unchanged, still never in frame (pull-back 0/120, CTA 0/155, closest 125 delivery px below the edge) — end-point call still open.
- Compute ~0.36 node-h total, one pass, no discards. Thermal: 720p runs the node hotter — peak 81.0 C, one >=80 off-time event (held to <=65, resumed 58.1 C), 48 pauses at the 75/70 gate.
- Report: files/v14-build/PREPASS-REPORT-R3.md; lessons table: files/v14-build/lessons-table.txt; stills: files/v14-build/stills-r3/.
