# C phext library: hashmap scroll store for compilation speed (F4)

Coordinate: 36.5.8/6.6.9/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): phcc should use the hashmap interface to speedup compilation, don't worry about working directly on the buffer most of the time
Status: Complete: F4 committed locally as e34c21f2 (not pushed). Hash-index store proven behaviour-identical (suite + fuzz + byte-identical driver outputs); lookups 2.5x on the real phcc.phext.

Notes:
- Base verified fresh via aletheia-core git SSH: wbic16/phcc main = exo = ef453cdc, tree 8c50e23e; all 584 tracked files blob-verified in the local work tree ~/workspace/phcc-hashmap/tree.
- Key design fact from the suite: the 163,831 checks pin phext_scrolls.items in sorted order (explode results and insert-built lists are compared element-wise), so F4 keeps the sorted array as the materialization/iteration order and makes the LOOKUP store a hash table — a lazily built open-addressing index over the items (splitmix64 chained over the 9 components, load <= 0.7, probe hits verified by coordinate equality, invalidated by any edit it cannot track exactly, binary search kept as the ENOMEM fallback). phext_implode already cloned+sorted before emitting, so byte-identical output is structural.
- Hash deliberately separate from the public FNV-1a phext_coordinate_hash (published values may be depended on; a table wants avalanche, not a stable value).

Results:
- Conformance (aletheia-core): parity suite 163,831 checks / 0 failures under gcc AND under phcc built from the tree (dogfood); phcc upstream make test ALL TESTS PASSED; ONE_SOURCE amalgamated build clean.
- Differential fuzz vs Rust reference driver: 40,000 cases (2 seeds x 20,000), 0 divergences on defined behaviour (Rust panics 173+166, all D-2 op-20 class). Stronger: new C driver outputs BYTE-IDENTICAL to pre-F4 driver on both corpora — nothing observable changed.
- Benchmark (aletheia-core, gcc -O2, medians of 7 interleaved runs; repo phcc.phext 49,209,925 B, sha256 646144c7…, explodes to 52,262 stored scrolls — parent brief said 52,815; measured store size in both binaries is 52,262; identical hit counts 180,163/200k and identical fetched bytes): gets_random 200k 21.6 ms -> 8.5 ms (2.5x, 108 -> 42 ns/get); gets_seq full pass 2.6 -> 1.9 ms (1.4x); one-time index build at first get 1.5 ms (break-even ~23k lookups); insert_shuffle build 539.7 -> 540.6 ms (parity — sorted memmove dominates both; F4 claims lookup speed, not insert speed); explode 42.0 -> 47.9 ms (no explode-path logic changed; relayout control build measured the same — attributed to code layout, reported not tuned).
- Docs: PARITY.md D-4 annotated SUPERSEDED (F4) + Outcome cross-ref; phext/README.md idiom row updated; PATCHES.md gains the F4 entry + per-file rows refreshed (phext.h +397, phext.c +2,031, PARITY.md +268).
- Committed LOCALLY only: e34c21f2 on ef453cdc in ~/workspace/phcc-hashmap/tree (5 files, +222/-15). NOT pushed — parent sequences the publish.
