Request (from session record): hard compatibility conformance with gcc, clang, and msvc.
Status: Slice 1 complete + placed in the phext (refresh e4407215, gate v8.1.0): corpus in Tests Book 11, REG-CONF-1/2 RESOLVED by F5 e399b212, conformance gate section live (328/333, 0 unclassified, MSVC NOT ATTESTED — Will attests manually at merge). OPEN FINDING from the refresh: phext Vol 2 snapshot predates F3/F4 (5 drifted files); carried tree unbuildable until a catch-up refresh of Makefile/PATCHES.md/libtcc1.c/libtcc.c/tcc.h — remedy verified (fixed tree make test ALL PASSED), awaiting parent scheduling.

Notes:
- Design: ~/workspace/goals/finish-phcc/files/phcc-conformance-design.md — claim, (a)/(b)/(c) classification with no-unclassified rule, tiers A/B/C, phext Book-11 corpus layout + report-only gate section designed (rides next gate version; no gate copy edited).
- MSVC (Will, 2026-11-07: "I'll confirm msvc compatibility manually when I merge."): the MSVC column is a manual attestation (signer Will Bickford + date + scope bound to manifest hash and phcc commit, T0-waiver pattern). Runner only emits NOT ATTESTED; never presented as an automated run; never in percentages.
- Windows (Will, 2026-11-07: "I'll be using phcc on Windows and Linux."): Windows x86_64 is a primary use platform; PE target, __declspec, MSVC-mode pragmas, SDK header compatibility are a named tier surface whose oracle is the manual attestation.
- Slice 1 ran on aletheia-core: gcc 13.3.0, clang 18.1.3 (verified present), phcc F3-state build (tcc 1.0.0 main@7573c4b8*, tree = ef453cdc).

Results:
- Matrix: 333 probes (A 289 / B 22 / C 22, incl. 3 negative). gcc==clang 333/333; three-way agreement 326/333; per tier A 288/289, B 16/22, C 22/22; 0 oracle splits, 0 unclassified divergences.
- DEFECT REG-CONF-1 (HIGH, silent): __attribute__((packed)) inert on ordinary structs — phcc 8/4 vs oracles 5/1 in all three placements and the __packed__ spelling; tcc-doc indexes packed as supported.
- DEFECT REG-CONF-2 (HIGH, silent): __attribute__((aligned(16))) inert — type 1/1 vs 16/16; aligned global placed at 8 mod 16 vs 0.
- Class (b): __STDC_VERSION__ 199901 vs 201710 (documented C99 dialect level; auto-reclassifies to (a) if C11/C17 claimed); _Complex unsupported (tcc-doc explicitly lists complex as missing; slice-1 Tier B inclusion corrected as scoping error); __builtin_bswap32/16 unresolved at link (absent from doc builtin list; link-time wart noted); __auto_type parse-rejected (unclaimed).
- Tier C: all 22 impl-defined catalogue items agree with both oracles (char signed, arithmetic right shift, long double 16/16, bitfield signedness, float macros...).
- Run-1 probe defects caught + fixed + disclosed (complex.h included in all B probes; unspecified arg evaluation order in a_atomic_004 caused the only oracle split). Headline numbers are run 2.
- Bindings: manifest sha256 c6eebb8a0146406373cb8bf9578455586148c696340f3b9b04c6dcbf63539cbb; results sha256 b3c23baef07298f7b9dea32475533f4bc59666f8814595c112daa3463027cf97 (byte-verified). Report: ~/workspace/phcc-conformance/REPORT.md. Nothing pushed; canonical phext untouched (Book-11 delta proposed in report).
